[{:db/id 17592186073738 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d90a8def-3584-5231-870a-71215d7b2ac3" "question-9df9f344-2897-5bbd-9091-a42a8b5a698c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073447 :question/problem "Which of the following ratios is equivalent to $12 : 9?$\n\nI. $2 : 3$\n\nII. $4 : 3$\n\nIII. $5 : 3$" :question/worked-solution "All of the answer choices have the second number equal to $3.$ So our equivalent ratio is of the form ![](images/35/35577ae6ed7f13a59f140d75fbd066251ec539423a5de48daa1736e7bbec25f8.svg)  \n\nTo find a ratio that's equivalent to $12 : 9,$ we divide both numbers by the same value. In particular, we need to get $3$ from ${\\color{red}{9}},$ so we divide ${\\color{red}{9}}$ by $3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{0}[/math]}} &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n So to get ![](images/21/211a836d739a9a5eadbaa452ad307a4d01d32818d1bd2ccee48eec256f64a2f0.svg) from ${\\color{blue}{12}},$ we divide $12$ by $3$ as well:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}12} \\div 3 =4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12:9$ is equivalent to $4:3.$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073739 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f79f6f3f-0665-5958-9f52-a760bcfd2aa5" "question-2c30cede-8611-5f0a-ae18-9d59bfca44eb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073448 :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $4$ triangles.\n\nThen, we count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $6$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to total shapes is $4:6.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in the ratio by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,2 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to the total shapes is $2:3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073740 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f982038d-d23d-5345-b398-01e403a579af" "question-8b912b09-6665-5b0d-812c-febdf9d9cbee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073449 :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d9f0a004ca9beb84b3a2a604d71dbf43ab70a67d899b167c5183ecc2ebe15f3.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of squares to circles is ![](images/29/296da85a5c6d0f5cf14f8fe144b0cdf66e4082b425b886d98fcbe672a2e8a190.svg) because there is $1$ square for every ![](images/b1/b1fda7079b1445faec7a1a2bb2abcafd9147f8a28863a2618c66166cea102a14.svg) circle(s)." :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of squares. We see that there are $2$ squares.\n\nThen, we count the number of circles. We see that there are $2$ circles.\n\nSo the ratio of circles to squares is $2:2.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $2:2$ is equivalent to $1:1.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of squares to circles is $1:\\bbox[3px,#d3d3d3]{1}\\,$ because there is $1$ square for every $\\bbox[3px,#d3d3d3]{1}\\,$circle.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-d90a8def-3584-5231-870a-71215d7b2ac3" :question/id #uuid "d90a8def-3584-5231-870a-71215d7b2ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-236323" :question/problem "The ratio $12:15$ is equivalent to the ratio{{field-1}}$:5.$" :question/worked-solution "To find a ratio that's equivalent to $12:15,$ we divide both numbers by the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,12 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\boxed{} &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get $5$ from $15,$ we divide $15$ by $3.$ So, to get $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ from $12,$ we divide $12$ by $3$ as well:\n\n$$\n12÷3=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12:15$ is equivalent to $4:5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-463c8835-db00-5463-a324-96a495b622bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-463c8835-db00-5463-a324-96a495b622bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "463c8835-db00-5463-a324-96a495b622bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b8727138-94be-5acc-8375-9ebb39076999" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8727138-94be-5acc-8375-9ebb39076999"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8727138-94be-5acc-8375-9ebb39076999" :answer/id #uuid "b8727138-94be-5acc-8375-9ebb39076999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9df9f344-2897-5bbd-9091-a42a8b5a698c" :question/id #uuid "9df9f344-2897-5bbd-9091-a42a8b5a698c" :question/math-academy-id "q-236318" :question/problem "The ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to the ratio $36:${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the ratio equivalent to $9:2$, we multiply both numbers by the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,9 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,36 &  & : &  & \\,\\boxed{} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get $36$ from $9,$ we multiply $9$ by $4.$ So, to get $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ from $2,$ we multiply $2$ by $4$ as well:\n\n$$\n4\\times 2=8\n$$\n\nThe ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to $36:8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c283c6a1-cc2d-5b83-baa1-16866a708164"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c283c6a1-cc2d-5b83-baa1-16866a708164" :answer-field/id #uuid "c283c6a1-cc2d-5b83-baa1-16866a708164" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5e64d548-40b5-52fc-b453-675de41c693a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e64d548-40b5-52fc-b453-675de41c693a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e64d548-40b5-52fc-b453-675de41c693a" :answer/id #uuid "5e64d548-40b5-52fc-b453-675de41c693a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f79f6f3f-0665-5958-9f52-a760bcfd2aa5" :question/id #uuid "f79f6f3f-0665-5958-9f52-a760bcfd2aa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-101451" :question/problem "![](images/79/79b659403c088680490bf308191be82b4acde242292210d15c1fb8525c7addfb.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of squares to the total number of shapes?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of squares. We see that there are $3$ squares.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $9$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of circles to total shapes is $3:9.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of squares to the total shapes is $1:3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc1ebd9a-4d55-5ce2-ab52-fd21dda2062f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc1ebd9a-4d55-5ce2-ab52-fd21dda2062f" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1ebd9a-4d55-5ce2-ab52-fd21dda2062f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72e3a14a-66f5-5604-b9c3-603dffacd9c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72e3a14a-66f5-5604-b9c3-603dffacd9c6" "answer-a5b648bc-a24c-5285-b13f-ad7aa8987e7a" "answer-8d7094a9-1172-5feb-b8cf-096197051ca5" "answer-e1a1b394-947b-5e5a-b6f9-9a12d5bb161b" "answer-b67ea84b-1222-5e4a-9ad1-d45c639a06fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72e3a14a-66f5-5604-b9c3-603dffacd9c6" :answer/id #uuid "72e3a14a-66f5-5604-b9c3-603dffacd9c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5b648bc-a24c-5285-b13f-ad7aa8987e7a" :answer/id #uuid "a5b648bc-a24c-5285-b13f-ad7aa8987e7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d7094a9-1172-5feb-b8cf-096197051ca5" :answer/id #uuid "8d7094a9-1172-5feb-b8cf-096197051ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1a1b394-947b-5e5a-b6f9-9a12d5bb161b" :answer/id #uuid "e1a1b394-947b-5e5a-b6f9-9a12d5bb161b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3:1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b67ea84b-1222-5e4a-9ad1-d45c639a06fd" :answer/id #uuid "b67ea84b-1222-5e4a-9ad1-d45c639a06fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3:4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c30cede-8611-5f0a-ae18-9d59bfca44eb" :question/id #uuid "2c30cede-8611-5f0a-ae18-9d59bfca44eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-92783" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1f62f15382a5f5d91ea1e2f56acc973d009316f62bdfd70f61fe131a28e42da1.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of rhombuses to the total number of shapes?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $4$ rhombuses.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $8$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to total shapes is $4:8.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,8 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rhombuses to the total shapes is $1:2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bada2b14-8923-50b6-a578-2ff2688ef53f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bada2b14-8923-50b6-a578-2ff2688ef53f" :answer-field/id #uuid "bada2b14-8923-50b6-a578-2ff2688ef53f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25b4050d-2855-552a-a59b-c2b4ec9e988f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25b4050d-2855-552a-a59b-c2b4ec9e988f" "answer-26f3ce87-0441-5aab-b938-80ad045e3822" "answer-821f0810-2be9-5e28-9ed8-277a2618152b" "answer-82572c7f-fe5e-5117-809e-0c1f1b0a3a0e" "answer-2eb20220-add6-5735-a22a-3c908dc65462"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25b4050d-2855-552a-a59b-c2b4ec9e988f" :answer/id #uuid "25b4050d-2855-552a-a59b-c2b4ec9e988f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26f3ce87-0441-5aab-b938-80ad045e3822" :answer/id #uuid "26f3ce87-0441-5aab-b938-80ad045e3822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-821f0810-2be9-5e28-9ed8-277a2618152b" :answer/id #uuid "821f0810-2be9-5e28-9ed8-277a2618152b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3:4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82572c7f-fe5e-5117-809e-0c1f1b0a3a0e" :answer/id #uuid "82572c7f-fe5e-5117-809e-0c1f1b0a3a0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2eb20220-add6-5735-a22a-3c908dc65462" :answer/id #uuid "2eb20220-add6-5735-a22a-3c908dc65462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5:8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f982038d-d23d-5345-b398-01e403a579af" :question/id #uuid "f982038d-d23d-5345-b398-01e403a579af" :question/math-academy-id "q-59907" :question/problem "A total of $25$ children and $10$ adults gathered for a charity event. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of children to adults is $5:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there were $5$ children for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ adults." :question/worked-solution "Since there are $25$ children and $10$ adults, the ratio of children to adults is $25:10.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,25 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,10 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,5 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $5:2$ is equivalent to $25:10.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of children to adults is $5:2\\,$ because there were $5$ children for every $2\\,$ adults.\"\n\nHence, the missing number is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51a6d4ad-11fe-5694-8867-69ac29e5267d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51a6d4ad-11fe-5694-8867-69ac29e5267d" :answer-field/id #uuid "51a6d4ad-11fe-5694-8867-69ac29e5267d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3419e825-6be0-56a4-9846-a9e56e53ce7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70c57267-c777-58cf-bf67-28641d3fbfe3" "answer-3419e825-6be0-56a4-9846-a9e56e53ce7e" "answer-cdb525e0-c07f-5b8c-a480-6c5f71a051bf" "answer-559ac78e-6367-5791-96ba-fc42656ba60a" "answer-34265f22-1ee0-5927-9535-d8bf181bf917"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70c57267-c777-58cf-bf67-28641d3fbfe3" :answer/id #uuid "70c57267-c777-58cf-bf67-28641d3fbfe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3419e825-6be0-56a4-9846-a9e56e53ce7e" :answer/id #uuid "3419e825-6be0-56a4-9846-a9e56e53ce7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdb525e0-c07f-5b8c-a480-6c5f71a051bf" :answer/id #uuid "cdb525e0-c07f-5b8c-a480-6c5f71a051bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-559ac78e-6367-5791-96ba-fc42656ba60a" :answer/id #uuid "559ac78e-6367-5791-96ba-fc42656ba60a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34265f22-1ee0-5927-9535-d8bf181bf917" :answer/id #uuid "34265f22-1ee0-5927-9535-d8bf181bf917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b912b09-6665-5b0d-812c-febdf9d9cbee" :question/id #uuid "8b912b09-6665-5b0d-812c-febdf9d9cbee" :question/math-academy-id "q-101458" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2fd396c9a62f29969acd4af3de44ac59dd4851a31b77e0c7902ab2e023942e31.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of heptagons to squares is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ heptagon for every $\\boxed{}$ squares." :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of heptagons. We see that there are $4$ heptagons.\n\nThen, we count the number of squares. We see that there are $4$ squares.\n\nSo the ratio of heptagons to squares is $4:4.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:1$ is equivalent to $4:4.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of heptagons to squares is $1:1$ because there is $1$ heptagon for every $1$ square.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a6dbb0b-b7b9-5f4e-9215-0a4dfc3abd68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a6dbb0b-b7b9-5f4e-9215-0a4dfc3abd68" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a6dbb0b-b7b9-5f4e-9215-0a4dfc3abd68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b242725a-ea8d-51d0-8958-60c3bc36261b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b242725a-ea8d-51d0-8958-60c3bc36261b" "answer-189ca1fc-d9bf-54e1-943e-8d472270ae3f" "answer-05bfa6a3-b567-5a5f-afbb-e5591b3e1ac6" "answer-0462ac67-14b3-5481-a443-957e97903cf8" "answer-d10c19cc-191b-5964-b066-73bf47f80d67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b242725a-ea8d-51d0-8958-60c3bc36261b" :answer/id #uuid "b242725a-ea8d-51d0-8958-60c3bc36261b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-189ca1fc-d9bf-54e1-943e-8d472270ae3f" :answer/id #uuid "189ca1fc-d9bf-54e1-943e-8d472270ae3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05bfa6a3-b567-5a5f-afbb-e5591b3e1ac6" :answer/id #uuid "05bfa6a3-b567-5a5f-afbb-e5591b3e1ac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0462ac67-14b3-5481-a443-957e97903cf8" :answer/id #uuid "0462ac67-14b3-5481-a443-957e97903cf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d10c19cc-191b-5964-b066-73bf47f80d67" :answer/id #uuid "d10c19cc-191b-5964-b066-73bf47f80d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075034 :tutorial/content "We can find **equivalent ratios** by multiplying or dividing all numbers in a ratio by the same value. \n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the following ratio:\n\n$$\n2:6\n$$\n\nIf we multiply *both* numbers by $5,$ for example, we get the ratio $10:30.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,6 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓\\times \\,5 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓\\times \\,5 &  \\\\ \\,10 &  & : &  & \\,30 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratios $2:6$ and $10:30$ are equivalent. \n\nSimilarly, if we take the ratio $2:6$ and divide *both* numbers by $2,$ we get $1:3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,6 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓÷\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratios  $2:6$ and  $1:3$ are also equivalent." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075035 :tutorial/content "Suppose that the following two ratios are equivalent:\n\n![](images/c6/c673bfcd099ef612f48bd0da7f8535cb9406d23088392e056884fb9415bb5100.svg)\n\nWhat is the missing number?\n\nTo find a ratio equivalent to $3 : 5,$ we multiply or divide both numbers by the same value. \n\nIn this case, we need to get $12$ from ${\\color{blue}{3}},$ so we multiply ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ by $4.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,5 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  \\\\ 12 &  & : &  & \\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{0}[/math]}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to get ![](images/50/50f3c1b8dc3b1628130d1de11abcc455fc22006f32b7486f658c8134fcc3221c.svg) from ${\\color{red}{5}},$ we multiply ${\\color{red}{5}}$ by $4$ as well: \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}5} \\times 4 = \\bbox[3px,lightgray]{\\color{red}20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $20.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075036 :tutorial/content "We can simplify ratios by dividing both numbers in the ratio by a common factor.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's simplify the following ratio: \n\n$$\n18:9\n$$\n\nThe numbers $18$ and $9$ share a common factor of $9,$ so we can divide both numbers by $9$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,18 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,9 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,2 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $18:9$ is equivalent to $2:1.$ \n\nSince $2$ and $1$ have no common factors, $2:1$ is the simplest form of this ratio. We often prefer to work with ratios in their simplest form, where possible." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073972 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
